      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.055,
            0.36,
            0.08
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "#Big O Cheat Sheet:"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.096,
            0.188,
            0.121
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "-Big Os-"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.137,
            0.281,
            0.155
          ],
          "content": "**O(1)** Constant- no loops"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.157,
            0.899,
            0.176
          ],
          "content": "**O(log N)** Logarithmic- usually searching algorithms have log n if they are sorted (Binary Search)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.178,
            0.511,
            0.197
          ],
          "content": "**O(n)** Linear- for loops, while loops through n items"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.199,
            0.515,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": "**O(n log(n))** Log Liniear- usually sorting operations"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.219,
            0.912,
            0.257
          ],
          "content": "**O(n^2)** Quadratic- every element in a collection needs to be compared to ever other element. Two nested loops"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.26,
            0.701,
            0.279
          ],
          "content": "**O(2^n)** Exponential- recursive algorithms that solves a problem of size N"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.281,
            0.556,
            0.3
          ],
          "content": "**O(n!)** Factorial- you are adding a loop for every element"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.316,
            0.505,
            0.334
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Iterating through half a collection is still O(n)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.336,
            0.39,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": "**Two separate collections: O(a \\* b)**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.372,
            0.589,
            0.395
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "-What can cause time in a function?-"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.413,
            0.252,
            0.431
          ],
          "content": "Operations (+, -, \\*, /)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.434,
            0.279,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": "Comparisons (<, >, ==)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.454,
            0.242,
            0.472
          ],
          "content": "Looping (for, while)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.474,
            0.356,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": "Outside Function call (function())"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.51,
            0.239,
            0.532
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "-Rule Book-"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.55,
            0.305,
            0.569
          ],
          "content": "**Rule 1:** Always worst Case"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.571,
            0.305,
            0.589
          ],
          "content": "**Rule 2:** Remove Constants"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.591,
            0.897,
            0.629
          ],
          "content": "**Rule 3:** Different inputs should have different variables. O(a+b). A and B arrays nested would be O(a\\*b)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.068,
            0.633,
            0.242,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": "\\+ for steps in order"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.653,
            0.225,
            0.671
          ],
          "content": "\\* for nested steps"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.067,
            0.674,
            0.368,
            0.692
          ],
          "content": "**Rule 4:** Drop Non-dominant terms"
        },
        {
